{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JbPu5GeE5rWXBkbVMRSX8D","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — irt_equated_bench_regen\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 (via ARR; long paper 8-page limit + unlimited refs)\n5\t- Page limit: 8 pages main text (当前 10 页，需压缩 2 页)\n6\t\n7\t## Paper Type\n8\tEmpirical analysis / psychometric characterization. Discovery paper, not methods paper. \"DIF reveals benchmark structural problems,\" not \"DIF detects contamination.\"\n9\t\n10\t## Core Claims (4 条, 可证伪)\n11\t\n12\t**Claim 1 (Temporal Comparability Concern)**: ~31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable across model generations — they exhibit large DIF (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5) between 2023 and 2024-H1 model cohorts. Primary estimate: **31.3%** (temporal cohort, plan_001). All 57 subjects show instability (C% range 20.7–48.4%, unweighted mean ≈30%, plan_001 domain_specificity.csv). Within-subject matching on 5 high-C% subjects yields higher rates (31-45%, avg 38.1%, plan_014) — report as robustness check, not primary. This instability is not a statistical artifact (random split sanity check: 0.18%), and correlates weakly with domain-specific accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307, p=0.02), but item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains only 2.4pp (7.6%). Architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue: METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227), excluding the 1 non-decoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0). Threshold sensitivity robustness confirmed: C% ranges from 48.9% (|Δ_MH|≥1.0) to 18.3% (|Δ_MH|≥2.0) to 10.2% (|Δ_MH|≥2.5). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 has negligible impact (removes 3/3,918 items).\n13\t- Evidence: plan_001 (C%=31.3%), plan_014 (within-subject C%=38.1%), plan_010 (arch-stratified: 99.98% decoder-only, C% unchanged, Jaccard=1.0), plan_018 (threshold: 49/31/18/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5; BH negligible), plan_019 (decomposition: ≤2.4pp/7.6% explained by domain improvement), plan_022 (model independence: graduated de-duplication to 1 model per family → C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap K; K=20: 29.1% vs random 30.9%, K=5: 11.7% vs random 16.9%; family structure does NOT inflate C%), plan_027 (temporal ability overlap: d=-0.17, OVL=76.4%; 1:1 NN matching C%=28.9%±0.1% vs full 31.3% — ability confound explains only 2.4pp; contrast with Llama-2v3 d=-0.99→matched C%=28.3%, where ability confound explains 33pp)\n14\t- Honesty requirement: ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) at subject level reflects a modest ecological correlation. Item-level decomposition (plan_019) shows domain improvement accounts for at most 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Caveat: item difficulty may be a mediator rather than confounder — use Model 1 as primary; Model 2 (Simpson's paradox) as supplementary.\n15\t- IRT fit: 98% of models show |Lz|>2, reflecting MMLU's inherent multidimensionality (57 subjects), not architecture heterogeneity. 1D IRT is fundamentally misspecified for MMLU — discuss in limitations as motivation for future multidimensional IRT work.\n16\t\n17\t**Claim 2 (Ground Truth Meta-critique)**: Existing contamination detection literature validates against web-overlap/n-gram labels that measure global exposure (whether an item is publicly accessible), not differential contamination (whether an item functions differently across model cohorts). DIF enrichment≈1.0 against Li et al. labels is expected, not failure — these labels cannot evaluate item-level differential detectors. This is a fundamental validation methodology gap: all work using web-overlap labels as ground truth for item-level detectors (including Min-K%, n-gram methods) has the same blind spot. **Empirically validated** (plan_026): direct comparison of DIF-C flags vs Li et al. web-overlap labels on 9,229 MMLU items shows enrichment=0.964, Jaccard=0.206, Phi=0.012, χ²=1.28 (p=0.258), OR=1.05 [0.96, 1.15]. Consistent across subtypes (input_only: 0.986, input_and_label: 0.960). Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF can detect differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5, dose-response from p=0.3 to p=1.0).\n18\t- Evidence: plan_001 (enrichment=0.96), plan_026 (direct comparison: enrichment=0.964, Jaccard=0.206, p=0.258), plan_011 (ΔTPR=+0.508, dose-response)\n19\t- Framing: aggressive — \"the field's standard validation approach is fundamentally mismatched for item-level detection\" — now with direct empirical evidence, not just conceptual argument\n20\t\n21\t**Claim 3 (Semi-synthetic Validation Framework)**: The ΔTPR methodology — injecting known differential contamination into real response matrices and measuring detection power increase — provides a controlled validation infrastructure for any item-level contamination detector. Cross-subject matching (using total score on OTHER subjects as MH matching variable) eliminates FPR inflation (ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 tested subjects), while within-subject matching suffers from matching variable contamination (FPR inflation +0.186).\n22\t- Evidence: plan_011, plan_016 (ΔFPR=0.000 cross-subject, 4/5 subjects ΔTPR>0.3), plan_004 Step 2 (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818 standard, +0.517 external)\n23\t- Cross-benchmark: GSM8K replication confirms framework portability to single-domain math benchmarks\n24\t- Positioning: cross-subject matching is a practical methodological recommendation; cross-benchmark replication strengthens generalizability\n25\t\n26\t**Claim 4 (Downstream Impact — Four-Layer Finding)**: DIF as diagnostic lens, not quality filter. Four sub-findings:\n27\t1. **Benchmark redundancy**: ρ≈0.997 between full and stable-only rankings — MMLU rankings are extremely robust to 31% item removal, revealing massive measurement redundancy in the benchmark.\n28\t2. **DIF items carry cross-cohort signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining items**: DIF removal causes MORE disruption than random removal (z=-8 to -49σ, 21/21 conditions), confirming DIF items are non-trivial. But circularity ablation (plan_020) shows DIF is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: accuracy-gap removal disrupts 10-16× more (z=-157 vs -9.5), high-variance 11× more (z=-108), high-discrimination 1.7× more (z=-16). MH's ability conditioning filters out raw accuracy differences, isolating genuine differential functioning rather than generally informative items. DIF-discrimination overlap is only 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) — DIF identifies \"items that changed across generations,\" not \"good items.\"\n29\t3. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF identifies which items' functioning changes most across model generations → reveals which capability dimensions drive ranking shifts. Not \"find bad items and remove\" but \"understand what changed and why.\" Model-specific patterns: phi-3/llama-3 gain +700-850 ranks from DIF items, mistral merges lose -400 to -587. **Item characterization** (plan_023): DIF-C items are moderately harder (Cohen's d=-0.247) and higher-discrimination (d=0.230) than non-DIF items, but uniformly distributed across MMLU domains (χ² p=0.32). Key finding: difficulty × DIF direction interaction (ρ=-0.597) — hardest-decile DIF-C items are 88.7% focal-favoring (2024 models do better), easiest-decile are 96.2% reference-favoring (2023 models do better). This reveals a systematic pattern: capability improvement concentrates on hard items, while easy items' difficulty structure erodes across generations.\n30\t4. **Cross-benchmark validation — DIF items resist contamination-based gains**: On GSM8K (1,319 items × 6,702 models), DIF flags anti-correlate with GSM1K contamination gap (r=−0.478, p=0.005, 95% BCa CI [−0.714, −0.155]; Spearman ρ=−0.403, p=0.020, CI [−0.687, −0.031]; partial r=−0.385 controlling GSM8K accuracy, p=0.030, CI [−0.640, −0.058]; permutation p=0.014). All CIs exclude zero. Models with larger contamination gaps show disproportionately lower performance on DIF-C items. This is consistent with contamination producing surface-level gains concentrated on non-DIF items, while DIF items capture genuine capability differences.\n31\t- Evidence: plan_017 (z=-8 to -49σ, ρ=0.996-0.999), plan_020 (circularity ablation: DIF z=-9.5 vs acc-gap z=-157, disc z=-16, var z=-108), plan_004 Step 3 (r=−0.478, p=0.005, N=33), plan_023 (item characterization: difficulty ρ=-0.597, domain uniformity χ² p=0.32)\n32\t- Architecture: plan_017 is load-bearing (strong, full N=5,227), Step 3 adds contamination dimension but is suggestive (N=33, CI wide). If Step 3 attacked, plan_017 stands independently.\n33\t- Growing Pains互补: \"Growing Pains uses anchor items for efficient evaluation; our DIF diagnostic tells them which anchor items are degrading\"\n34\t- Caveats (→ limitations): N=33, Pearson CI upper bound |r|=0.155 (small effect possible), Spearman CI upper bound |ρ|=0.031 (near zero possible); item difficulty confound not fully excluded (DIF-C items harder for all models); contamination gap is proxy, not ground truth; replication with larger matched sample needed\n35\t\n36\t## Story Spine (v2 — no-pivot narrative)\n37\t\n38\t**Opening frame**: LLM benchmarks implicitly assume temporal score comparability — when we say \"Model B outperforms Model A on MMLU,\" we presume both scores reflect the same latent construct. But do they? Psychometrics has a mature tool for testing exactly this: Differential Item Functioning (DIF) analysis detects items whose difficulty changes across examinee groups after controlling for overall ability. We apply MH-DIF to the METABENCH response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items) — the largest-scale DIF analysis on LLM benchmarks to date.\n39\t\n40\t**Key narrative principle**: \"Instability ≠ invalidity.\" DIF flags items whose functioning changed across generations — this is a diagnostic signal, not a quality verdict. MMLU rankings are massively redundant (ρ≈0.997 after removing 31% of items), so instability doesn't threaten validity. But it reveals WHICH capability dimensions are shifting. **This framing must appear in the Introduction, not be deferred to Discussion.**\n41\t\n42\t**What we find** (4 contributions, focused):\n43\t\n44\t1. **31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable** across model generations (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5). Robust to threshold choice (49%/31%/18%/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5), multiple testing (BH removes 3/3918 items), and architecture composition (99.98% decoder-only). Domain accuracy improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific, not a proxy for \"models got better.\"\n45\t\n46\t2. **Ground truth meta-critique**: Web-overlap contamination labels measure global exposure, not differential contamination. Enrichment≈1.0 is expected. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF detects differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508). Any item-level detector validated against web-overlap labels has this blind spot.\n47\t\n48\t3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework**: ΔTPR methodology with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). Portable across benchmarks (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818). Reusable for validating any item-level contamination detector.\n49\t\n50\t4. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF items carry cross-cohort signal (z=-8 to -49σ vs random) but are the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy (z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157). DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just informative items. Cross-benchmark: DIF items resist contamination-based gains (r=−0.478, BCa CI [−0.71, −0.16]).\n51\t\n52\t**Headline result**: \"Psychometric DIF analysis of 5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items reveals 31% temporal instability — robust across thresholds, not driven by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and not a validity threat (ρ≈0.997 ranking stability). The field's web-overlap ground truth cannot capture this differential signal; we provide a semi-synthetic validation framework with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). DIF items resist contamination-based gains (r=−0.478) and serve as a diagnostic lens for understanding what changed across model generations.\"\n53\t\n54\t## Scope Control (main body vs appendix)\n55\t\n56\t**MAIN BODY (4 claims + robustness)**:\n57\t- §1 Introduction (problem + \"instability ≠ invalidity\" framing upfront)\n58\t- §2 Related Work (45 papers, 5 clusters)\n59\t- §3 Method (MH-DIF primer, semi-synthetic framework, cross-subject matching)\n60\t- §4 Experiments: Claim 1 (temporal DIF + threshold + BH + decomposition + architecture), Claim 2 (enrichment + meta-critique), Claim 3 (semi-synthetic + cross-benchmark), Claim 4 (redundancy + circularity ablation + diagnostic lens + GSM1K validation)\n61\t- §5 Discussion + Limitations\n62\t- §6 Conclusion\n63\t\n64\t**APPENDIX (pruned from main body)**:\n65\t- Bayesian cumulative DIF (plan_007) — simulation-only, underdeveloped\n66\t- RL robustness (plan_002) — N=13, underpowered\n67\t- Ensemble fusion (plan_003a/b/c) — negative, not executed\n68\t- Bifactor equating pilot — below target fit\n69\t- Item generation pilot — below benchmarks\n70\t- Graceful degradation — clean but supplementary\n71\t- Item-Focused Trees — robustness check, supplementary\n72\t- ConStat/DVD comparisons — complementary baselines\n73\t\n74\t## Empirical Observation: Structural Constraints on DIF in LLM Benchmarks\n75\t\n76\tSystematic experimentation reveals that three structural improvements — matched-ability cohort design (plan_001b), IRT θ-conditioning (plan_012, r=0.9986), and bifactor pre-check (plan_014, within-subject C%=38.1%) — all fail to reduce temporal DIF baseline FPR below 31% while maintaining detection power. This is an empirical observation, not a formal impossibility result. The constraints arise from: (a) unidimensional IRT limitations in modeling 57-subject multidimensional ability, (b) statistical power requirements (N≥80, δ≥1.4), and (c) inability to separate ability confounding from genuine item-level changes. Higher-level methods (MIMIC, propensity-score matching, multidimensional IRT) may address individual constraints — future work.\n77\t\n78\t## Venue Fit\n79\t\n80\t- **EMNLP 2026**: Strong fit — NLP evaluation methodology is a dedicated area, reviewers expect empirical studies of benchmarks. \"Empirical, not algorithmic\" contribution type well-received. Risk: 8-page limit requires significant compression (current 10 pages). Mitigation: move structural analysis details to appendix.\n81\t\n82\t## Novelty Articulation (三层，显式化)\n83\t\n84\tMH-DIF (1959/1988) is applied without modification. **Explicitly acknowledge this.** Novelty is NOT algorithmic. Three layers of genuine contribution:\n85\t\n86\t1. **Empirical discovery at unprecedented scale**: First DIF analysis on 5,227×12,508 LLM response matrix. Finding: 31% temporal instability is robust across thresholds (10-49%), not explained by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and architecturally homogeneous (99.98% decoder-only). No prior work has characterized item-level stability of LLM benchmarks at this scale. The instability finding itself is new data about MMLU's measurement properties.\n87\t\n88\t2. **Ground truth meta-critique with field-wide implications**: The observation that web-overlap labels cannot validate item-level differential detectors is NOT obvious — the field routinely uses them. This affects the validity claims of Min-K%, ConStat, n-gram methods, and all papers using web-overlap as ground truth. First empirical demonstration (enrichment≈1.0 + semi-synthetic proof).\n89\t\n90\t3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework + cross-subject matching**: The ΔTPR methodology is a reusable infrastructure contribution. Cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000) is a novel practical innovation — the insight that within-subject matching contaminates the conditioning variable is subtle and general. Portable to any multi-domain benchmark (demonstrated on GSM8K).\n91\t\n92\t**Framing**: \"We bring mature psychometric tools to characterize an urgent ML evaluation problem. The contribution is the empirical findings, the validation methodology critique, and the reusable framework — not a new algorithm.\"\n93\t\n94\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns (updated for pivot)\n95\t\n96\t1. **\"31% could just mean models got better / ability confound inflates C%\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_019 + plan_027). Item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). Temporal cohort ability gap is negligible (d=-0.17, OVL=76.4%); 1:1 NN matching (d≈-0.01) yields C%=28.9%±0.1% vs full 31.3% — ability confound explains only 2.4pp. Contrast: Llama-2v3 (d=-0.99) drops from 61.3% to 28.3% under matching. Both converge to ~28-29% genuine item-level DIF.\n97\t\n98\t2. **\"Ground truth critique is obvious — of course web labels don't capture differential effects\"** — Not obvious: the field routinely uses these labels for item-level validation. We provide the first empirical demonstration with both the enrichment≈1.0 result and the semi-synthetic proof of concept.\n99\t\n100\t3. **\"Semi-synthetic injection is artificial\"** — We inject into real response matrices (not simulated), preserving real ability distributions and item characteristics. The mechanism (incorrect→correct flipping) is a simplification acknowledged in limitations.\n101\t\n102\t4. **\"DIF power is only sufficient for large effects\"** — Large effects are precisely what threaten benchmark validity most. Operational region: N≥80, δ≥1.4, TPR=0.68-0.80.\n103\t\n104\t5. **\"Only validated on MMLU\"** — Partially addressed: GSM8K replication (METABENCH 1,319 items × 6,702 models) confirms semi-synthetic framework portability (ΔTPR=+0.818) and temporal DIF pattern (C%=18.9%). GSM1K contamination gap validation (N=33) provides cross-benchmark evidence. Full generalization to diverse benchmarks remains future work.\n105\t\n106\t6. **\"Higher methods (MIMIC, propensity-score) could solve the confounding\"** — Acknowledged as future work. We frame our three-attempt negative results as \"empirical observation\" that motivates these directions, not as impossibility.\n107\t\n108\t7. **\"ETS threshold is uncalibrated for LLM populations\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). C% at {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5} = {48.9%, 31.3%, 18.3%, 10.2%}. Finding >15% holds at standard thresholds [1.0, 2.0]. At conservative 2.5, still 10.2% (1,278 items). Present as: \"finding is robust across standard thresholds; even at the most conservative cutoff, >10% of items show large DIF.\" Do NOT claim \">15% at all thresholds\" — be honest that 2.5 drops below.\n109\t\n110\t8. **\"Multiple testing: 12,508 simultaneous tests without correction\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 removes only 3/3,918 ETS C items (31.32%→31.30%). At higher thresholds, BH impact is zero. ETS dual requirement (effect size + significance) provides near-complete implicit protection. Random-split sanity check (C%=0.18%) confirms empirically.\n111\t\n112\t9. **\"Only uniform DIF — non-uniform DIF plausible for LLMs\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_021). LR-DIF on 9 subjects (1787 items): MH C-class 92.1% concordance with LR uniform DIF → MH detection robust. Non-uniform DIF: 38.7% at significance threshold, **24.8% at |β_interaction|≥0.5** (conservative, effect-size controlled). MH structurally underestimates instability. Caveat: LR used within-subject matching (vs MH's cross-benchmark), so 38.7% may be inflated; use 24.8% in paper. Framing: \"our 31% uniform-only estimate is conservative.\"\n113\t\n114\t10. **\"5,227 models are not independent — fine-tunes/merges inflate N and DIF significance\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_022). Graduated de-duplication (capping models per family at K=1,2,5,10,20) shows C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap: K=20 (447 models) C%=29.1% vs random 30.9%; K=5 (146 models) C%=11.7% vs random 16.9%; K=1 (33 families) C%=0.17% (underpowered, N<80). Family structure does NOT inflate C% — if anything, de-duplication reduces it slightly less than random subsampling. The 31.3% figure is robust to model non-independence.\n115\t\n116\t11. **\"Ranking disruption result is tautological\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_020). Circularity ablation shows DIF removal is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157, discrimination z=-16, variance z=-108. Despite 62.6% item overlap with accuracy-gap selection, MH ability conditioning makes DIF 10-16× less disruptive. DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just items with large raw group differences. Tautology refuted.\n117\t\n118\t## Dropped from Original Framing\n119\t\n120\t- **Ensemble (Claim 2 old)**: plan_003a/b/c never executed. Future work.\n121\t- **Regeneration (Claim 3 old)**: Bifactor killed by plan_014 pre-check. Dropped entirely.\n122\t- **RL robustness**: Theoretically motivated but N=13 insufficient. Limitations disclosure, not claim.\n123\t- **Detection as primary contribution**: Pivoted from \"we detect contamination\" to \"we characterize benchmark properties.\"\n124\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec5f3729-5afa-4d81-a1f7-4323c92a2cff","uuid":"22bb0335-b6aa-4f08-a126-45945b506fa6","timestamp":"2026-05-21T09:21:16.031Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T085919/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — irt_equated_bench_regen\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 (via ARR; long paper 8-page limit + unlimited refs)\n- Page limit: 8 pages main text (当前 10 页，需压缩 2 页)\n\n## Paper Type\nEmpirical analysis / psychometric characterization. Discovery paper, not methods paper. \"DIF reveals benchmark structural problems,\" not \"DIF detects contamination.\"\n\n## Core Claims (4 条, 可证伪)\n\n**Claim 1 (Temporal Comparability Concern)**: ~31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable across model generations — they exhibit large DIF (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5) between 2023 and 2024-H1 model cohorts. Primary estimate: **31.3%** (temporal cohort, plan_001). All 57 subjects show instability (C% range 20.7–48.4%, unweighted mean ≈30%, plan_001 domain_specificity.csv). Within-subject matching on 5 high-C% subjects yields higher rates (31-45%, avg 38.1%, plan_014) — report as robustness check, not primary. This instability is not a statistical artifact (random split sanity check: 0.18%), and correlates weakly with domain-specific accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307, p=0.02), but item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains only 2.4pp (7.6%). Architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue: METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227), excluding the 1 non-decoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0). Threshold sensitivity robustness confirmed: C% ranges from 48.9% (|Δ_MH|≥1.0) to 18.3% (|Δ_MH|≥2.0) to 10.2% (|Δ_MH|≥2.5). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 has negligible impact (removes 3/3,918 items).\n- Evidence: plan_001 (C%=31.3%), plan_014 (within-subject C%=38.1%), plan_010 (arch-stratified: 99.98% decoder-only, C% unchanged, Jaccard=1.0), plan_018 (threshold: 49/31/18/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5; BH negligible), plan_019 (decomposition: ≤2.4pp/7.6% explained by domain improvement), plan_022 (model independence: graduated de-duplication to 1 model per family → C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap K; K=20: 29.1% vs random 30.9%, K=5: 11.7% vs random 16.9%; family structure does NOT inflate C%), plan_027 (temporal ability overlap: d=-0.17, OVL=76.4%; 1:1 NN matching C%=28.9%±0.1% vs full 31.3% — ability confound explains only 2.4pp; contrast with Llama-2v3 d=-0.99→matched C%=28.3%, where ability confound explains 33pp)\n- Honesty requirement: ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) at subject level reflects a modest ecological correlation. Item-level decomposition (plan_019) shows domain improvement accounts for at most 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Caveat: item difficulty may be a mediator rather than confounder — use Model 1 as primary; Model 2 (Simpson's paradox) as supplementary.\n- IRT fit: 98% of models show |Lz|>2, reflecting MMLU's inherent multidimensionality (57 subjects), not architecture heterogeneity. 1D IRT is fundamentally misspecified for MMLU — discuss in limitations as motivation for future multidimensional IRT work.\n\n**Claim 2 (Ground Truth Meta-critique)**: Existing contamination detection literature validates against web-overlap/n-gram labels that measure global exposure (whether an item is publicly accessible), not differential contamination (whether an item functions differently across model cohorts). DIF enrichment≈1.0 against Li et al. labels is expected, not failure — these labels cannot evaluate item-level differential detectors. This is a fundamental validation methodology gap: all work using web-overlap labels as ground truth for item-level detectors (including Min-K%, n-gram methods) has the same blind spot. **Empirically validated** (plan_026): direct comparison of DIF-C flags vs Li et al. web-overlap labels on 9,229 MMLU items shows enrichment=0.964, Jaccard=0.206, Phi=0.012, χ²=1.28 (p=0.258), OR=1.05 [0.96, 1.15]. Consistent across subtypes (input_only: 0.986, input_and_label: 0.960). Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF can detect differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5, dose-response from p=0.3 to p=1.0).\n- Evidence: plan_001 (enrichment=0.96), plan_026 (direct comparison: enrichment=0.964, Jaccard=0.206, p=0.258), plan_011 (ΔTPR=+0.508, dose-response)\n- Framing: aggressive — \"the field's standard validation approach is fundamentally mismatched for item-level detection\" — now with direct empirical evidence, not just conceptual argument\n\n**Claim 3 (Semi-synthetic Validation Framework)**: The ΔTPR methodology — injecting known differential contamination into real response matrices and measuring detection power increase — provides a controlled validation infrastructure for any item-level contamination detector. Cross-subject matching (using total score on OTHER subjects as MH matching variable) eliminates FPR inflation (ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 tested subjects), while within-subject matching suffers from matching variable contamination (FPR inflation +0.186).\n- Evidence: plan_011, plan_016 (ΔFPR=0.000 cross-subject, 4/5 subjects ΔTPR>0.3), plan_004 Step 2 (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818 standard, +0.517 external)\n- Cross-benchmark: GSM8K replication confirms framework portability to single-domain math benchmarks\n- Positioning: cross-subject matching is a practical methodological recommendation; cross-benchmark replication strengthens generalizability\n\n**Claim 4 (Downstream Impact — Four-Layer Finding)**: DIF as diagnostic lens, not quality filter. Four sub-findings:\n1. **Benchmark redundancy**: ρ≈0.997 between full and stable-only rankings — MMLU rankings are extremely robust to 31% item removal, revealing massive measurement redundancy in the benchmark.\n2. **DIF items carry cross-cohort signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining items**: DIF removal causes MORE disruption than random removal (z=-8 to -49σ, 21/21 conditions), confirming DIF items are non-trivial. But circularity ablation (plan_020) shows DIF is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: accuracy-gap removal disrupts 10-16× more (z=-157 vs -9.5), high-variance 11× more (z=-108), high-discrimination 1.7× more (z=-16). MH's ability conditioning filters out raw accuracy differences, isolating genuine differential functioning rather than generally informative items. DIF-discrimination overlap is only 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) — DIF identifies \"items that changed across generations,\" not \"good items.\"\n3. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF identifies which items' functioning changes most across model generations → reveals which capability dimensions drive ranking shifts. Not \"find bad items and remove\" but \"understand what changed and why.\" Model-specific patterns: phi-3/llama-3 gain +700-850 ranks from DIF items, mistral merges lose -400 to -587. **Item characterization** (plan_023): DIF-C items are moderately harder (Cohen's d=-0.247) and higher-discrimination (d=0.230) than non-DIF items, but uniformly distributed across MMLU domains (χ² p=0.32). Key finding: difficulty × DIF direction interaction (ρ=-0.597) — hardest-decile DIF-C items are 88.7% focal-favoring (2024 models do better), easiest-decile are 96.2% reference-favoring (2023 models do better). This reveals a systematic pattern: capability improvement concentrates on hard items, while easy items' difficulty structure erodes across generations.\n4. **Cross-benchmark validation — DIF items resist contamination-based gains**: On GSM8K (1,319 items × 6,702 models), DIF flags anti-correlate with GSM1K contamination gap (r=−0.478, p=0.005, 95% BCa CI [−0.714, −0.155]; Spearman ρ=−0.403, p=0.020, CI [−0.687, −0.031]; partial r=−0.385 controlling GSM8K accuracy, p=0.030, CI [−0.640, −0.058]; permutation p=0.014). All CIs exclude zero. Models with larger contamination gaps show disproportionately lower performance on DIF-C items. This is consistent with contamination producing surface-level gains concentrated on non-DIF items, while DIF items capture genuine capability differences.\n- Evidence: plan_017 (z=-8 to -49σ, ρ=0.996-0.999), plan_020 (circularity ablation: DIF z=-9.5 vs acc-gap z=-157, disc z=-16, var z=-108), plan_004 Step 3 (r=−0.478, p=0.005, N=33), plan_023 (item characterization: difficulty ρ=-0.597, domain uniformity χ² p=0.32)\n- Architecture: plan_017 is load-bearing (strong, full N=5,227), Step 3 adds contamination dimension but is suggestive (N=33, CI wide). If Step 3 attacked, plan_017 stands independently.\n- Growing Pains互补: \"Growing Pains uses anchor items for efficient evaluation; our DIF diagnostic tells them which anchor items are degrading\"\n- Caveats (→ limitations): N=33, Pearson CI upper bound |r|=0.155 (small effect possible), Spearman CI upper bound |ρ|=0.031 (near zero possible); item difficulty confound not fully excluded (DIF-C items harder for all models); contamination gap is proxy, not ground truth; replication with larger matched sample needed\n\n## Story Spine (v2 — no-pivot narrative)\n\n**Opening frame**: LLM benchmarks implicitly assume temporal score comparability — when we say \"Model B outperforms Model A on MMLU,\" we presume both scores reflect the same latent construct. But do they? Psychometrics has a mature tool for testing exactly this: Differential Item Functioning (DIF) analysis detects items whose difficulty changes across examinee groups after controlling for overall ability. We apply MH-DIF to the METABENCH response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items) — the largest-scale DIF analysis on LLM benchmarks to date.\n\n**Key narrative principle**: \"Instability ≠ invalidity.\" DIF flags items whose functioning changed across generations — this is a diagnostic signal, not a quality verdict. MMLU rankings are massively redundant (ρ≈0.997 after removing 31% of items), so instability doesn't threaten validity. But it reveals WHICH capability dimensions are shifting. **This framing must appear in the Introduction, not be deferred to Discussion.**\n\n**What we find** (4 contributions, focused):\n\n1. **31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable** across model generations (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5). Robust to threshold choice (49%/31%/18%/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5), multiple testing (BH removes 3/3918 items), and architecture composition (99.98% decoder-only). Domain accuracy improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific, not a proxy for \"models got better.\"\n\n2. **Ground truth meta-critique**: Web-overlap contamination labels measure global exposure, not differential contamination. Enrichment≈1.0 is expected. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF detects differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508). Any item-level detector validated against web-overlap labels has this blind spot.\n\n3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework**: ΔTPR methodology with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). Portable across benchmarks (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818). Reusable for validating any item-level contamination detector.\n\n4. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF items carry cross-cohort signal (z=-8 to -49σ vs random) but are the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy (z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157). DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just informative items. Cross-benchmark: DIF items resist contamination-based gains (r=−0.478, BCa CI [−0.71, −0.16]).\n\n**Headline result**: \"Psychometric DIF analysis of 5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items reveals 31% temporal instability — robust across thresholds, not driven by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and not a validity threat (ρ≈0.997 ranking stability). The field's web-overlap ground truth cannot capture this differential signal; we provide a semi-synthetic validation framework with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). DIF items resist contamination-based gains (r=−0.478) and serve as a diagnostic lens for understanding what changed across model generations.\"\n\n## Scope Control (main body vs appendix)\n\n**MAIN BODY (4 claims + robustness)**:\n- §1 Introduction (problem + \"instability ≠ invalidity\" framing upfront)\n- §2 Related Work (45 papers, 5 clusters)\n- §3 Method (MH-DIF primer, semi-synthetic framework, cross-subject matching)\n- §4 Experiments: Claim 1 (temporal DIF + threshold + BH + decomposition + architecture), Claim 2 (enrichment + meta-critique), Claim 3 (semi-synthetic + cross-benchmark), Claim 4 (redundancy + circularity ablation + diagnostic lens + GSM1K validation)\n- §5 Discussion + Limitations\n- §6 Conclusion\n\n**APPENDIX (pruned from main body)**:\n- Bayesian cumulative DIF (plan_007) — simulation-only, underdeveloped\n- RL robustness (plan_002) — N=13, underpowered\n- Ensemble fusion (plan_003a/b/c) — negative, not executed\n- Bifactor equating pilot — below target fit\n- Item generation pilot — below benchmarks\n- Graceful degradation — clean but supplementary\n- Item-Focused Trees — robustness check, supplementary\n- ConStat/DVD comparisons — complementary baselines\n\n## Empirical Observation: Structural Constraints on DIF in LLM Benchmarks\n\nSystematic experimentation reveals that three structural improvements — matched-ability cohort design (plan_001b), IRT θ-conditioning (plan_012, r=0.9986), and bifactor pre-check (plan_014, within-subject C%=38.1%) — all fail to reduce temporal DIF baseline FPR below 31% while maintaining detection power. This is an empirical observation, not a formal impossibility result. The constraints arise from: (a) unidimensional IRT limitations in modeling 57-subject multidimensional ability, (b) statistical power requirements (N≥80, δ≥1.4), and (c) inability to separate ability confounding from genuine item-level changes. Higher-level methods (MIMIC, propensity-score matching, multidimensional IRT) may address individual constraints — future work.\n\n## Venue Fit\n\n- **EMNLP 2026**: Strong fit — NLP evaluation methodology is a dedicated area, reviewers expect empirical studies of benchmarks. \"Empirical, not algorithmic\" contribution type well-received. Risk: 8-page limit requires significant compression (current 10 pages). Mitigation: move structural analysis details to appendix.\n\n## Novelty Articulation (三层，显式化)\n\nMH-DIF (1959/1988) is applied without modification. **Explicitly acknowledge this.** Novelty is NOT algorithmic. Three layers of genuine contribution:\n\n1. **Empirical discovery at unprecedented scale**: First DIF analysis on 5,227×12,508 LLM response matrix. Finding: 31% temporal instability is robust across thresholds (10-49%), not explained by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and architecturally homogeneous (99.98% decoder-only). No prior work has characterized item-level stability of LLM benchmarks at this scale. The instability finding itself is new data about MMLU's measurement properties.\n\n2. **Ground truth meta-critique with field-wide implications**: The observation that web-overlap labels cannot validate item-level differential detectors is NOT obvious — the field routinely uses them. This affects the validity claims of Min-K%, ConStat, n-gram methods, and all papers using web-overlap as ground truth. First empirical demonstration (enrichment≈1.0 + semi-synthetic proof).\n\n3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework + cross-subject matching**: The ΔTPR methodology is a reusable infrastructure contribution. Cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000) is a novel practical innovation — the insight that within-subject matching contaminates the conditioning variable is subtle and general. Portable to any multi-domain benchmark (demonstrated on GSM8K).\n\n**Framing**: \"We bring mature psychometric tools to characterize an urgent ML evaluation problem. The contribution is the empirical findings, the validation methodology critique, and the reusable framework — not a new algorithm.\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns (updated for pivot)\n\n1. **\"31% could just mean models got better / ability confound inflates C%\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_019 + plan_027). Item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). Temporal cohort ability gap is negligible (d=-0.17, OVL=76.4%); 1:1 NN matching (d≈-0.01) yields C%=28.9%±0.1% vs full 31.3% — ability confound explains only 2.4pp. Contrast: Llama-2v3 (d=-0.99) drops from 61.3% to 28.3% under matching. Both converge to ~28-29% genuine item-level DIF.\n\n2. **\"Ground truth critique is obvious — of course web labels don't capture differential effects\"** — Not obvious: the field routinely uses these labels for item-level validation. We provide the first empirical demonstration with both the enrichment≈1.0 result and the semi-synthetic proof of concept.\n\n3. **\"Semi-synthetic injection is artificial\"** — We inject into real response matrices (not simulated), preserving real ability distributions and item characteristics. The mechanism (incorrect→correct flipping) is a simplification acknowledged in limitations.\n\n4. **\"DIF power is only sufficient for large effects\"** — Large effects are precisely what threaten benchmark validity most. Operational region: N≥80, δ≥1.4, TPR=0.68-0.80.\n\n5. **\"Only validated on MMLU\"** — Partially addressed: GSM8K replication (METABENCH 1,319 items × 6,702 models) confirms semi-synthetic framework portability (ΔTPR=+0.818) and temporal DIF pattern (C%=18.9%). GSM1K contamination gap validation (N=33) provides cross-benchmark evidence. Full generalization to diverse benchmarks remains future work.\n\n6. **\"Higher methods (MIMIC, propensity-score) could solve the confounding\"** — Acknowledged as future work. We frame our three-attempt negative results as \"empirical observation\" that motivates these directions, not as impossibility.\n\n7. **\"ETS threshold is uncalibrated for LLM populations\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). C% at {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5} = {48.9%, 31.3%, 18.3%, 10.2%}. Finding >15% holds at standard thresholds [1.0, 2.0]. At conservative 2.5, still 10.2% (1,278 items). Present as: \"finding is robust across standard thresholds; even at the most conservative cutoff, >10% of items show large DIF.\" Do NOT claim \">15% at all thresholds\" — be honest that 2.5 drops below.\n\n8. **\"Multiple testing: 12,508 simultaneous tests without correction\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 removes only 3/3,918 ETS C items (31.32%→31.30%). At higher thresholds, BH impact is zero. ETS dual requirement (effect size + significance) provides near-complete implicit protection. Random-split sanity check (C%=0.18%) confirms empirically.\n\n9. **\"Only uniform DIF — non-uniform DIF plausible for LLMs\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_021). LR-DIF on 9 subjects (1787 items): MH C-class 92.1% concordance with LR uniform DIF → MH detection robust. Non-uniform DIF: 38.7% at significance threshold, **24.8% at |β_interaction|≥0.5** (conservative, effect-size controlled). MH structurally underestimates instability. Caveat: LR used within-subject matching (vs MH's cross-benchmark), so 38.7% may be inflated; use 24.8% in paper. Framing: \"our 31% uniform-only estimate is conservative.\"\n\n10. **\"5,227 models are not independent — fine-tunes/merges inflate N and DIF significance\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_022). Graduated de-duplication (capping models per family at K=1,2,5,10,20) shows C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap: K=20 (447 models) C%=29.1% vs random 30.9%; K=5 (146 models) C%=11.7% vs random 16.9%; K=1 (33 families) C%=0.17% (underpowered, N<80). Family structure does NOT inflate C% — if anything, de-duplication reduces it slightly less than random subsampling. The 31.3% figure is robust to model non-independence.\n\n11. **\"Ranking disruption result is tautological\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_020). Circularity ablation shows DIF removal is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157, discrimination z=-16, variance z=-108. Despite 62.6% item overlap with accuracy-gap selection, MH ability conditioning makes DIF 10-16× less disruptive. DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just items with large raw group differences. Tautology refuted.\n\n## Dropped from Original Framing\n\n- **Ensemble (Claim 2 old)**: plan_003a/b/c never executed. Future work.\n- **Regeneration (Claim 3 old)**: Bifactor killed by plan_014 pre-check. Dropped entirely.\n- **RL robustness**: Theoretically motivated but N=13 insufficient. Limitations disclosure, not claim.\n- **Detection as primary contribution**: Pivoted from \"we detect contamination\" to \"we characterize benchmark properties.\"\n","numLines":124,"startLine":1,"totalLines":124}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JupbKfBs5gXwDfQpsA4RGC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"real_data_dif_mmlu\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"MH-DIF analysis on METABENCH MMLU (5,227 models × 12,508 items). Temporal cohort (2023 vs 2024-H1), ability-quintile split, Li et al. proxy validation, within-family confound control, domain-specificity analysis.\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"temporal_ets_c_pct\": 31.3,\n7\t      \"temporal_fpr_li_clean\": 0.318,\n8\t      \"temporal_enrichment\": 0.96,\n9\t      \"ability_ets_c_pct\": 2.9,\n10\t      \"ability_enrichment\": 1.19,\n11\t      \"within_family_llama2v3_c_pct\": 61.3,\n12\t      \"within_family_mistral_mixtral_c_pct\": 38.7,\n13\t      \"domain_spearman_rho\": 0.307,\n14\t      \"domain_spearman_p\": 0.02,\n15\t      \"sanity_random_split_c_pct\": 0.18,\n16\t      \"temporal_ability_jaccard\": 0.014\n17\t    },\n18\t    \"tables\": [\n19\t      \"Table 1: Temporal DIF Summary — C/B/A 分布 across 12,508 items\",\n20\t      \"Table 2: Cohort × DIF cross-tabulation (2023 N=1,080 vs 2024 N=807)\",\n21\t      \"Table 3: Domain-specificity — top/bottom 10 subjects by C%\"\n22\t    ],\n23\t    \"figures\": [],\n24\t    \"analysis\": \"这是论文的核心实验，在 median 档完全成立。31.3% C% 经受住了所有 robustness 检验（阈值、 多重检验、架构、能力分解、模型独立性）。审稿人的主要挑战不在于数字本身，而在于 \\\"31% instability 意味着什么\\\"——是否有 actionable 的下游影响。enrichment≈0.96 对 Claim 2 来说是关键证据，但在 median 档审稿人可能认为这个 null result 本身并不令人惊讶。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，31.3% 核心发现成立并通过审稿。时间队列 DIF 反映了真实的 item 功能变化， 而非统计伪迹（随机分割仅 0.18%）。Li et al. 标签的 enrichment≈0.96 确认了 web-overlap 标签 与 DIF 正交——这在 median 档被接受为预期结果而非 DIF 失败的证据。能力五分位 C%=2.9% 远低于 时间队列的 31.3%，证明 DIF 信号是时间效应而非能力分层伪迹。within-family Llama-2v3 的 C%=61.3% 较高因为能力差距大（d=-0.99），但在 plan_027 匹配后降至 28.3%。 domain ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) 表示领域改进与 DIF 有弱关联，但 plan_019 分解证明仅解释 2.4pp。 审稿人接受该发现为稳健的，但一位审稿人质疑 ETS C 的 |Δ_MH|≥1.5 阈值是否适合 LLM 人群， 要求看不同阈值下的结果（引向 plan_018）。\\n\"\n25\t  },\n26\t  {\n27\t    \"name\": \"rl_robustness_validation\",\n28\t    \"description\": \"验证 DIF 对 RL 训练模型的鲁棒性。在 METABENCH 中分离 SFT-only、alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO)、 reasoning-RL (GRPO/PPO) 模型，比较 DIF 检测一致性。\\n\",\n29\t    \"results\": {\n30\t      \"sft_only_cohort_n\": 312,\n31\t      \"alignment_rl_cohort_n\": 477,\n32\t      \"reasoning_rl_n_available\": 13,\n33\t      \"dif_flag_jaccard_sft_vs_alignrl\": 0.72,\n34\t      \"dif_flag_jaccard_sft_vs_full\": 0.85,\n35\t      \"reasoning_rl_added_c_pct_change\": -0.4,\n36\t      \"constat_auroc_on_sft\": 0.68,\n37\t      \"constat_auroc_on_rl\": 0.53,\n38\t      \"mink_auroc_on_sft\": 0.61,\n39\t      \"mink_auroc_on_rl\": 0.47,\n40\t      \"tost_equivalence_dif_retention\": \"p=0.08, inconclusive\",\n41\t      \"bootstrap_ci_auroc_diff_dif_vs_constat\": \"[-0.05, 0.18]\"\n42\t    },\n43\t    \"tables\": [\n44\t      \"Table: DIF flag overlap across SFT/alignment-RL/reasoning-RL cohort compositions\",\n45\t      \"Table: Per-detector AUROC comparison (DIF vs ConStat vs Min-K%) across model types\"\n46\t    ],\n47\t    \"figures\": [],\n48\t    \"analysis\": \"N=13 reasoning-RL 模型是不可克服的瓶颈。在 median 档审稿人接受 alignment-RL 部分但 认为核心 claim（DIF 对 reasoning-RL 鲁棒）未被验证。这个实验最终不进入 main body， 在 limitations 中提及为\\\"initial evidence, insufficient for formal claim\\\"。 GPU 预算 100h 大部分用于推理 10-15 个开源 GRPO/PPO 模型跑 MMLU，结果数据量不够 支撑统计检验。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，DIF 对 alignment-RL 模型表现稳定（Jaccard=0.72），因为 DPO/ORPO 不改变 NLL gap 结构。但 reasoning-RL 样本仅 13 个模型，严重不足以支撑任何统计结论。 将 13 个 reasoning-RL 模型加入 focal 队列后 C% 变化仅 -0.4pp，技术上\\\"稳健\\\"但 审稿人正确指出这不等于验证——13 个模型被 800+ 其他模型淹没。TOST 等价性检验 不显著（p=0.08），留下不确定性。传统检测器（ConStat、Min-K%）在 RL 模型上 AUROC 下降约 0.10-0.15，但 CI 宽，bootstrap 差异含零。 在 median 档这个实验被认为\\\"不够有力\\\"——N=13 reasoning-RL 的限制被视为致命缺陷， 整个 RL robustness 论述被降级为 future work 而非正式 claim。\\n\"\n49\t  },\n50\t  {\n51\t    \"name\": \"constat_perturbation_eval\",\n52\t    \"description\": \"独立评估 ConStat 式 perturbation testing 在 MMLU 上的检测能力。 生成 200+ MMLU 题目的语义等价改写，比较原始/改写表现，FDR 控制检测。\\n\",\n53\t    \"results\": {\n54\t      \"n_items_reformulated\": 237,\n55\t      \"n_models_tested\": 50,\n56\t      \"perturbation_detection_rate_overall\": 0.14,\n57\t      \"perturbation_detection_rate_suspected_contaminated\": 0.23,\n58\t      \"perturbation_detection_rate_clean\": 0.09,\n59\t      \"fdr_controlled_detections\": 34,\n60\t      \"mean_accuracy_drop_original_to_perturbed\": 0.031,\n61\t      \"mean_accuracy_drop_suspected\": 0.058,\n62\t      \"mean_accuracy_drop_clean\": 0.012,\n63\t      \"constat_dif_flag_overlap_jaccard\": 0.11\n64\t    },\n65\t    \"tables\": [\n66\t      \"Table: ConStat detection rates by contamination status (Li et al. labels)\",\n67\t      \"Table: ConStat vs DIF flag confusion matrix\"\n68\t    ],\n69\t    \"figures\": [],\n70\t    \"analysis\": \"ConStat 在 MMLU 上表现不佳的根本原因是 MMLU 的 4-choice MCQ 格式限制了 perturbation 效果。改写后语义保持但表面形式变化有限，模型的正确率下降不够大。在 median 档 审稿人可能质疑 perturbation 质量，但更根本的问题是 ConStat 设计用于检测 verbatim 记忆而非 differential functioning，所以低 overlap 是 expected 而非 failure。 这个实验消耗 80h GPU 但产出有限，属于 negative-but-informative result。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，ConStat 式方法在 MMLU 4 选 1 格式上受限——perturbation 空间受限于 问题改写而非选项重排（MMLU 选项本身是固定的），导致 signal 较弱。 整体检测率仅 14%，在疑似污染 items 上稍高（23%）但仍远低于 DIF 的 31.3%。 accuracy drop 均值仅 3.1pp，信噪比低。ConStat 与 DIF 标记的 Jaccard=0.11 极低， 验证了两种方法捕获不同维度的信号——ConStat 检测个体模型的 verbatim 记忆， DIF 检测群体层面的差异功能。这个结果在 median 档被认为\\\"有信息量但不 compelling\\\"， 最终作为 baseline comparison 放入 appendix/supplementary 而非 main body。\\n\"\n71\t  },\n72\t  {\n73\t    \"name\": \"dvd_generation_variance_eval\",\n74\t    \"description\": \"独立评估 DVD generation variance 在 MMLU 上的检测能力。 10-15 个开源模型每题生成 50 次 response，计算 generation variance，检测双峰分布。\\n\",\n75\t    \"results\": {\n76\t      \"n_models_tested\": 12,\n77\t      \"n_items_evaluated\": 12508,\n78\t      \"bimodal_detection_rate\": 0.07,\n79\t      \"bimodal_on_dif_c_items\": 0.09,\n80\t      \"bimodal_on_non_dif_items\": 0.06,\n81\t      \"variance_score_dif_c_mean\": 0.342,\n82\t      \"variance_score_non_dif_mean\": 0.318,\n83\t      \"variance_diff_effect_size_d\": 0.12,\n84\t      \"dvd_dif_overlap_jaccard\": 0.04\n85\t    },\n86\t    \"tables\": [\n87\t      \"Table: Generation variance summary statistics by DIF category\"\n88\t    ],\n89\t    \"figures\": [],\n90\t    \"analysis\": \"DVD 在 MCQ 上的理论限制是预期内的——generation variance 对 MCQ 格式本身不适配。 这 70h GPU 产出 negative result，在论文中仅作为一句话提及（\\\"DVD generation variance is designed for open-ended tasks and shows near-zero signal on MCQ benchmarks\\\"）。 审稿人不会挑战这个结论，但也不会因此给分。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，DVD generation variance 在 MMLU 上表现最差。4-choice MCQ 的 generation variance 本质上受限于离散分布——模型要么选对要么选错，temperature sampling 在 MCQ 上产生的 variance 主要反映模型 confidence 而非 contamination signal。 bimodal 检测率仅 7%，DIF-C 与 non-DIF items 差异极小（d=0.12），overlap Jaccard=0.04 说明两种方法几乎完全独立。DVD 设计初衷是开放生成任务（如代码生成），在 MCQ 上 先天不适用。在 median 档这个结果迅速确认 DVD 不适用于 MMLU 评估，实验结论明确但 对论文贡献有限。\\n\"\n91\t  },\n92\t  {\n93\t    \"name\": \"ensemble_fusion\",\n94\t    \"description\": \"融合 DIF + ConStat + DVD 为多信号集成检测器。2-of-3 majority voting 和加权融合。\\n\",\n95\t    \"results\": {\n96\t      \"ensemble_attempted\": false,\n97\t      \"reason\": \"plan_003a 和 plan_003b 个体信号太弱，无法构建有意义的集成\",\n98\t      \"constat_standalone_auroc\": 0.58,\n99\t      \"dvd_standalone_auroc\": 0.52,\n100\t      \"dif_standalone_auroc\": \"N/A (group-level, not model-level)\",\n101\t      \"notes\": \"DIF 是群体层面方法，无法与 ConStat/DVD 在 item-model 粒度融合\"\n102\t    },\n103\t    \"tables\": [],\n104\t    \"figures\": [],\n105\t    \"analysis\": \"Ensemble fusion 的失败不是实验失败而是概念重构——认识到 DIF 和 per-model detectors 回答不同问题（\\\"which items function differently\\\" vs \\\"which models memorized\\\"）。 这个认识反而强化了 Claim 2（meta-critique），因为它揭示了粒度不匹配问题。 在 median 档，审稿人不会批评未做的集成，因为论文已经 pivot 到 diagnostic lens 叙事。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，ensemble fusion 因为两个根本问题而未完成：(1) plan_003a 和 plan_003b 的个体信号太弱（ConStat AUROC≈0.58, DVD AUROC≈0.52），集成无法从噪声中提取 信号；(2) 更根本的是，DIF 是群体层面方法（检测 item 在两个群体间的差异功能）， 而 ConStat/DVD 是模型层面方法（检测单个模型的记忆），粒度不匹配导致融合框架 概念上不连贯。在 median 档这个实验被正确放弃，论文叙事从 \\\"ensemble detection\\\" 转向 \\\"DIF as diagnostic lens\\\"，避免了强行融合不可融合的方法。\\n\"\n106\t  },\n107\t  {\n108\t    \"name\": \"cross_benchmark_gsm8k\",\n109\t    \"description\": \"在 GSM8K 上复制 DIF 分析，使用 GSM1K 作为 contamination ground truth。 三步：(1) GSM8K temporal DIF, (2) semi-synthetic validation, (3) GSM1K 相关。\\n\",\n110\t    \"results\": {\n111\t      \"step1_gsm8k_temporal_c_pct\": 18.9,\n112\t      \"step1_n_items\": 1319,\n113\t      \"step1_sanity_c_pct\": 0.3,\n114\t      \"step2_standard_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.818,\n115\t      \"step2_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.517,\n116\t      \"step3_n_models\": 33,\n117\t      \"step3_pearson_r\": -0.478,\n118\t      \"step3_pearson_p\": 0.005,\n119\t      \"step3_spearman_rho\": -0.403,\n120\t      \"step3_spearman_p\": 0.02,\n121\t      \"step3_partial_r\": -0.385,\n122\t      \"step3_partial_p\": 0.027,\n123\t      \"step3_bca_ci_pearson\": \"[-0.714, -0.155]\",\n124\t      \"step3_bca_ci_spearman\": \"[-0.687, -0.031]\",\n125\t      \"step3_permutation_p\": 0.014,\n126\t      \"step3_cook_d_max\": \"Deepseek-math-7b-rl\",\n127\t      \"step3_leave_one_out_r_range\": \"[-0.537, -0.374]\"\n128\t    },\n129\t    \"tables\": [\n130\t      \"Table: GSM8K temporal DIF summary (1,319 items × 6,702 models)\",\n131\t      \"Table: Semi-synthetic ΔTPR dose-response on GSM8K\",\n132\t      \"Table: GSM1K correlation statistics with CIs (moved to appendix in median)\"\n133\t    ],\n134\t    \"figures\": [],\n135\t    \"analysis\": \"GSM8K 复制的 Step 1+2 在 median 档完全成立并进入 main body。Step 3 是 median 档 最大的弱点之一——N=33, wide CIs, causal ambiguity。在 rebuttal 中不应试图捍卫 Step 3 的 headline 地位，而应主动将其定位为 \\\"preliminary cross-benchmark evidence that motivates larger-scale replication\\\"。这样做既诚实又保护了论文的 credibility。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，GSM8K Step 1 和 Step 2 成功复制——temporal C%=18.9% 低于 MMLU 的 31.3%（合理，GSM8K 是单一数学领域，能力结构更均质），semi-synthetic ΔTPR=0.818 确认框架跨 benchmark 可移植性。\\n关键争议在 Step 3：r=-0.478 (p=0.005) 看似显著，但 N=33 导致 CI 极宽—— Pearson CI 上界 |r|=0.155 意味着真实效应可能很小，Spearman CI 上界 |ρ|=0.031 意味着几乎可以为零。在 median 档，至少一位审稿人指出：(a) N=33 严重不足， (b) GSM1K contamination gap 本身是 proxy 而非 ground truth，(c) 反向相关的 因果解释不唯一——DIF-C items 可能仅因为更难而使 contaminated 模型在上面得分低。\\n审稿人建议将 Step 3 从 headline results 降级为 supplementary evidence。这与 median 档的 \\\"GSM1K correlation is discounted\\\" 假设一致。论文将 Step 3 用作 \\\"suggestive cross-benchmark evidence\\\" 而非 \\\"confirmation of contamination resistance\\\"。\\n\"\n136\t  },\n137\t  {\n138\t    \"name\": \"bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\",\n139\t    \"description\": \"在 METABENCH MMLU 上拟合 bifactor IRT 模型（general factor + 57 subject-specific factors）， 选择 anchor items，通过 fixed-parameter calibration 进行 equating。\\n\",\n140\t    \"results\": {\n141\t      \"bifactor_convergence\": false,\n142\t      \"convergence_attempts\": 3,\n143\t      \"partial_fit_5_subjects_rmsea\": 0.089,\n144\t      \"partial_fit_5_subjects_cfi\": 0.71,\n145\t      \"partial_fit_5_subjects_srmr\": 0.112,\n146\t      \"full_57_factor_status\": \"non-convergence after 5000 EM iterations\",\n147\t      \"anchor_item_selection\": \"N/A — model did not converge\",\n148\t      \"equating_completed\": false\n149\t    },\n150\t    \"tables\": [],\n151\t    \"figures\": [],\n152\t    \"analysis\": \"Bifactor 失败是 median 档 \\\"Claim 3 (regeneration) dropped entirely\\\" 的直接原因。 没有 bifactor equating，就没有 principled 的 anchor item 选择方法，整个 regeneration pipeline 缺乏基础。这个 negative result 对论文 framing 的影响是积极的—— 它迫使论文从 \\\"we can fix benchmarks\\\" 转向 \\\"we can diagnose benchmarks\\\"， 后者更诚实也更 defensible。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，bifactor IRT 在 MMLU 上面临两个结构性障碍：(1) 57 个 subject-specific factors 的参数空间巨大（12,508 items × 58 factors），EM 算法在 5,227 个 models 上 无法收敛；(2) 即使在 5 个 subjects 子集上部分拟合，fit indices 也不达标 （RMSEA>0.08, CFI<0.90），因为 MMLU 本身是知识测验而非心理测量量表——item 之间 的 local independence 假设被 subject 内的 topic clustering 严重违反。 plan_013 的 Q3 分析已显示 within-subject 有 11.3% 的 item pairs 违反 local independence。 bifactor 模型无法修复这个根本问题。实验被 kill 前仅消耗约 15h GPU（远低于 50h 预算）， 合理止损。在 median 档论文将此作为 limitations 中 \\\"empirical observation\\\" 的一部分， motivation for future multidimensional IRT work。\\n\"\n153\t  },\n154\t  {\n155\t    \"name\": \"item_generation_calibration\",\n156\t    \"description\": \"为 DIF-flagged MMLU 题目生成替代题目，通过 student simulation 进行难度校准。\\n\",\n157\t    \"results\": {\n158\t      \"experiment_executed\": false,\n159\t      \"reason\": \"plan_005 (bifactor IRT) failed — no calibration targets available\",\n160\t      \"dependency_chain_broken\": true\n161\t    },\n162\t    \"tables\": [],\n163\t    \"figures\": [],\n164\t    \"analysis\": \"Plan_006 的缺失不影响 median 档论文质量——paper 已 pivot away from regeneration。 但审稿人中有一位可能会问 \\\"so what should practitioners do with these DIF flags?\\\" without replacement items, the answer is weak. This is one of the 1-2 claims needing softening in median tier — the diagnostic lens framing needs a concrete protocol (DIF audit checklist) to fill the actionability gap.\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，plan_005 的失败导致 plan_006 从未启动。没有 bifactor 模型提供的 item parameter targets，LLM 生成的替代题目无法与原始题目在 IRT 参数空间对齐。 仅靠 CTT difficulty (p-value) 匹配不足以保证 construct equivalence。 这 200h GPU 预算完全未使用。论文中不提及此实验（未执行 = 无结果可报告）， 但 regeneration 方向作为 \\\"promising future work\\\" 出现在 conclusion 中。\\n\"\n165\t  },\n166\t  {\n167\t    \"name\": \"cumulative_bayesian_dif\",\n168\t    \"description\": \"实现 Sinharay et al. (2006) 累积贝叶斯 DIF 先验。模拟 4 次连续 benchmark administration，展示累积证据下的 power 提升。\\n\",\n169\t    \"results\": {\n170\t      \"simulation_only\": true,\n171\t      \"single_admin_power_delta_10\": 0.42,\n172\t      \"cumulative_2_admin_power\": 0.58,\n173\t      \"cumulative_3_admin_power\": 0.71,\n174\t      \"cumulative_4_admin_power\": 0.79,\n175\t      \"effect_size_simulated\": 1.0,\n176\t      \"n_per_admin\": 100,\n177\t      \"prior_shrinkage_on_small_effects\": 0.35,\n178\t      \"bayesian_fpr_vs_frequentist\": \"0.028 vs 0.042\"\n179\t    },\n180\t    \"tables\": [\n181\t      \"Table (Appendix): Power by # administrations × effect size (simulation grid)\"\n182\t    ],\n183\t    \"figures\": [],\n184\t    \"analysis\": \"Cumulative Bayesian DIF 在 median 档被视为 \\\"nice to have\\\" 而非必要。审稿人不会 批评这个 idea 本身，但会认为没有 real-data validation 就无法支撑论文 claim。 零 GPU 消耗（纯模拟），投入产出比合理作为 supplementary material。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，cumulative Bayesian DIF 是纯模拟实验，展示理论上的 power 提升： 单次 administration 对 medium effects (δ=1.0) 的 power 仅 0.42，但 3 次累积后 达到 0.71——超过了 MH 在 N=80, δ=1.4 时的 0.68。Bayesian shrinkage 还将小效应 的 FPR 从 0.042 降至 0.028。但这全部是模拟结果，没有在 METABENCH 真实数据上 验证（因为只有 2 个时间点，不够 4 次 administration）。在 median 档审稿人承认 理论价值但认为 \\\"simulation without real validation is supplementary at best\\\"。 这个实验被放入 appendix，作为 future monitoring framework 的理论基础。\\n\"\n185\t  },\n186\t  {\n187\t    \"name\": \"graceful_degradation_analysis\",\n188\t    \"description\": \"分析 benchmark 在 item 替换下的 validity degradation。 定义 validity metrics，模拟渐进替换（5%-50%），建立理论 bounds。\\n\",\n189\t    \"results\": {\n190\t      \"replacement_items_available\": false,\n191\t      \"degradation_only_analysis\": true,\n192\t      \"removal_5pct_rho\": 0.9994,\n193\t      \"removal_10pct_rho\": 0.9987,\n194\t      \"removal_20pct_rho\": 0.9971,\n195\t      \"removal_31pct_rho\": 0.9965,\n196\t      \"removal_50pct_rho\": 0.9921,\n197\t      \"shr_degradation_31pct\": -0.0015,\n198\t      \"construct_coverage_31pct\": \"54/57 subjects retained ≥70% items\"\n199\t    },\n200\t    \"tables\": [\n201\t      \"Table (Appendix): Ranking stability (ρ) and SHR as function of removal rate\"\n202\t    ],\n203\t    \"figures\": [],\n204\t    \"analysis\": \"Graceful degradation 的核心发现已被 plan_017 部分报告。独立贡献有限但强化了 \\\"MMLU is massively redundant\\\" 的论点。在 median 档这作为 supplementary evidence 支持 Claim 4a (benchmark redundancy) 但不改变审稿评分。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，由于 plan_005/006 失败，无替代 items 可用，graceful degradation 只能分析 removal（不含 replacement）。结果高度积极：即使移除 31% DIF-C items， ranking stability 仍 ρ=0.9965——这直接支撑了 \\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\" narrative。 50% 移除后仍 ρ>0.99，证明 MMLU 有极大的 measurement redundancy。\\n但这个分析本质上与 plan_017 高度重叠（plan_017 已报告 ρ=0.996-0.999）。 在 median 档审稿人不会为 redundant results 给额外分数。graceful degradation 的独特贡献——construct coverage 分析（54/57 subjects retain ≥70% items）—— 是一个 small addition，放入 appendix。\\n\"\n205\t  },\n206\t  {\n207\t    \"name\": \"item_focused_trees\",\n208\t    \"description\": \"实现 Tutz & Berger (2016) Item-Focused Trees，将 model release date 作为 连续协变量替代 categorical cohort DIF。\\n\",\n209\t    \"results\": {\n210\t      \"n_items_analyzed\": 12508,\n211\t      \"ift_flagged_items_pct\": 28.7,\n212\t      \"ift_mh_c_overlap_jaccard\": 0.61,\n213\t      \"ift_unique_flags_pct\": 4.2,\n214\t      \"mh_unique_flags_pct\": 6.8,\n215\t      \"temporal_trend_significant_items_pct\": 22.3,\n216\t      \"linear_trend_dominant\": true,\n217\t      \"nonlinear_trend_items_pct\": 6.4,\n218\t      \"advantage_over_mh\": \"avoids arbitrary cohort boundary; captures gradual drift\",\n219\t      \"disadvantage_vs_mh\": \"computationally expensive; interpretation less transparent\"\n220\t    },\n221\t    \"tables\": [\n222\t      \"Table (Appendix): MH vs IFT flag comparison — 2×2 contingency table\"\n223\t    ],\n224\t    \"figures\": [],\n225\t    \"analysis\": \"IFT 确认 MH 发现的 robustness 但不改变结论。在 median 档审稿人可能欣赏方法论 thoroughness 但不会因此提高 novelty 评分。零 GPU 消耗，作为 supplementary 的 cost-benefit 比合理。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，IFT 提供了 DIF 的连续视角——28.7% items 被标记，与 MH 的 31.3% 有 Jaccard=0.61 的重叠。IFT 额外发现 4.2% 的 items 有 gradual drift 但未达 MH 的 C 阈值（effect 在 B 区间逐渐累积），同时 MH 标记的 6.8% items 在 IFT 中 不显著（可能是 MH 对 cohort boundary 的特殊性敏感）。22.3% 的 items 显示 statistically significant 的时间趋势（非平坦 ICCs across release dates）。\\n在 median 档审稿人认为 IFT 是 \\\"interesting robustness check\\\" 但不构成独立贡献—— 核心发现（~30% items 功能不稳定）无论用 MH 还是 IFT 都成立。IFT 的计算成本 （每个 item 一棵 tree，12,508 棵）远高于 MH，但额外信息有限。 放入 appendix 作为 method robustness 证据。\\n\"\n226\t  },\n227\t  {\n228\t    \"name\": \"architecture_stratified_dif\",\n229\t    \"description\": \"在 architecture-homogeneous (decoder-only) 子群上运行 DIF，检验 IRT 模型拟合 是否改善、spurious DIF 是否减少。\\n\",\n230\t    \"results\": {\n231\t      \"decoder_only_n\": 5226,\n232\t      \"decoder_only_pct\": 99.98,\n233\t      \"non_decoder_n\": 1,\n234\t      \"c_pct_decoder_only\": 31.3,\n235\t      \"c_pct_full\": 31.3,\n236\t      \"jaccard_decoder_vs_full\": 1.0,\n237\t      \"rpb_mean_decoder\": 0.3993,\n238\t      \"rpb_mean_full\": 0.3993,\n239\t      \"lz_misfit_pct_decoder\": 98.0,\n240\t      \"lz_misfit_pct_full\": 98.0\n241\t    },\n242\t    \"tables\": [\n243\t      \"Table: Architecture composition of METABENCH MMLU\",\n244\t      \"Table: DIF results comparison — full vs decoder-only (identical)\"\n245\t    ],\n246\t    \"figures\": [],\n247\t    \"analysis\": \"Plan_010 的结果在 median 档是 strong defense against a weak attack——architecture heterogeneity 从未真正是个问题因为数据集本身就是 homogeneous。但作为 proactive defense（提前排除审稿人可能的 concern），这是 good practice。结果进入 main body 作为一句话 + footnote：\\\"METABENCH is 99.98% decoder-only (5,226/5,227); excluding the one non-decoder model yields identical results (Jaccard=1.0).\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，architecture stratification 产生了最 anticlimactic 但最 clean 的 结果：METABENCH MMLU 中 99.98% 的模型是 decoder-only，仅 1 个 encoder-decoder 模型 (AurelPx/Pegasus-7b-slerp)。移除它后所有指标完全不变——C% 相同， Jaccard=1.0，rpb 分布相同，person misfit 相同。这彻底排除了 architecture heterogeneity 作为 DIF 伪迹来源。\\n但同时暴露了一个 separate 问题：98% 的模型 |Lz|>2 表明 1D IRT 本身对 MMLU 严重 misspecified——这不是 architecture 的问题，而是 MMLU 57 subjects 的 多维性本身。在 median 档审稿人接受 architecture 不是问题，但可能追问 \\\"if 98% of models misfit the IRT model, how valid are MH results at all?\\\" 论文回应：MH 不依赖 IRT model fit，它直接条件化 total score，是非参数方法。 Lz misfit 是 IRT 的问题，不是 MH 的问题。这个辩护在 median 档被接受但留 lingering doubt。\\n\"\n248\t  },\n249\t  {\n250\t    \"name\": \"semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\",\n251\t    \"description\": \"在真实 METABENCH response matrix 中注入已知 contamination，测量 DIF 检测力。 变化注入参数：contamination prevalence, exploitation rate, focal group size。\\n\",\n252\t    \"results\": {\n253\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p0\": 0.326,\n254\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p03\": 0.548,\n255\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p05\": 0.834,\n256\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p07\": 0.99,\n257\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p10\": 1.0,\n258\t      \"temporal_external_fpr\": 0.314,\n259\t      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508,\n260\t      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.674,\n261\t      \"standard_mh_fpr_inflation_at_p10\": 0.616,\n262\t      \"cross_subject_matching_fpr_stable\": true,\n263\t      \"cross_subject_delta_fpr\": 0.0,\n264\t      \"within_subject_fpr_inflation_p10\": 0.186,\n265\t      \"dose_response_monotonic\": true,\n266\t      \"n_clean_items\": 500,\n267\t      \"n_injected_items\": 200\n268\t    },\n269\t    \"tables\": [\n270\t      \"Table: ΔTPR dose-response across exploitation rates p ∈ {0, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 1.0}\",\n271\t      \"Table: FPR comparison — standard vs cross-subject vs within-subject matching\"\n272\t    ],\n273\t    \"figures\": [],\n274\t    \"analysis\": \"Semi-synthetic validation 在 median 档是论文中技术最 clean 的贡献。cross-subject matching 的 ΔFPR=0.000 结果是 elegant 的，提供了 concrete methodological recommendation。 但 \\\"niche\\\" 评价意味着这个贡献的 impact 被 discount——EMNLP 审稿人期望看到 broader implications for the NLP community, not just psychometric methodology refinement。 在 rebuttal 中应强调 framework 的 reusability：any future item-level detector can use this semi-synthetic protocol for controlled validation。\\n\\n在 median 档，semi-synthetic 实验是 Claim 3 的核心证据，成功展示了三个关键结果： (1) DIF 对 injected contamination 有明确的 dose-response（ΔTPR 从 p=0.3 到 p=1.0 单调增加），证明 DIF 能够检测 differential contamination； (2) cross-subject matching 完全消除 FPR inflation（ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 tested subjects），而 standard/within-subject matching 导致 FPR 从 0.30 膨胀到 0.62—— 这是 matching variable contamination 效应的直接证明； (3) 基线 FPR=0.314 接近 plan_001 的 temporal C%=31.3%，这不是巧合——它反映了 真实数据中已存在的 temporal DIF（注入在 existing DIF 之上叠加）。\\n在 median 档，至少一位审稿人欣赏 cross-subject matching 的 innovation（\\\"subtle and general insight about matching variable contamination\\\"），但另一位认为 semi-synthetic injection 过于简化（\\\"incorrect→correct flipping doesn't model real contamination mechanisms\\\"）。论文在 limitations 中 acknowledge 这一点。 Semi-synthetic framework 被一位审稿人视为 \\\"useful but niche\\\"——对 DIF 研究者有价值 但对一般 NLP 社区影响有限。\\n\"\n275\t  }\n276\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec5f3729-5afa-4d81-a1f7-4323c92a2cff","uuid":"e7ac3d1f-156f-46cf-8926-9211d80555fb","timestamp":"2026-05-21T09:21:16.374Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T085919/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"real_data_dif_mmlu\",\n    \"description\": \"MH-DIF analysis on METABENCH MMLU (5,227 models × 12,508 items). Temporal cohort (2023 vs 2024-H1), ability-quintile split, Li et al. proxy validation, within-family confound control, domain-specificity analysis.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"temporal_ets_c_pct\": 31.3,\n      \"temporal_fpr_li_clean\": 0.318,\n      \"temporal_enrichment\": 0.96,\n      \"ability_ets_c_pct\": 2.9,\n      \"ability_enrichment\": 1.19,\n      \"within_family_llama2v3_c_pct\": 61.3,\n      \"within_family_mistral_mixtral_c_pct\": 38.7,\n      \"domain_spearman_rho\": 0.307,\n      \"domain_spearman_p\": 0.02,\n      \"sanity_random_split_c_pct\": 0.18,\n      \"temporal_ability_jaccard\": 0.014\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 1: Temporal DIF Summary — C/B/A 分布 across 12,508 items\",\n      \"Table 2: Cohort × DIF cross-tabulation (2023 N=1,080 vs 2024 N=807)\",\n      \"Table 3: Domain-specificity — top/bottom 10 subjects by C%\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是论文的核心实验，在 median 档完全成立。31.3% C% 经受住了所有 robustness 检验（阈值、 多重检验、架构、能力分解、模型独立性）。审稿人的主要挑战不在于数字本身，而在于 \\\"31% instability 意味着什么\\\"——是否有 actionable 的下游影响。enrichment≈0.96 对 Claim 2 来说是关键证据，但在 median 档审稿人可能认为这个 null result 本身并不令人惊讶。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，31.3% 核心发现成立并通过审稿。时间队列 DIF 反映了真实的 item 功能变化， 而非统计伪迹（随机分割仅 0.18%）。Li et al. 标签的 enrichment≈0.96 确认了 web-overlap 标签 与 DIF 正交——这在 median 档被接受为预期结果而非 DIF 失败的证据。能力五分位 C%=2.9% 远低于 时间队列的 31.3%，证明 DIF 信号是时间效应而非能力分层伪迹。within-family Llama-2v3 的 C%=61.3% 较高因为能力差距大（d=-0.99），但在 plan_027 匹配后降至 28.3%。 domain ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) 表示领域改进与 DIF 有弱关联，但 plan_019 分解证明仅解释 2.4pp。 审稿人接受该发现为稳健的，但一位审稿人质疑 ETS C 的 |Δ_MH|≥1.5 阈值是否适合 LLM 人群， 要求看不同阈值下的结果（引向 plan_018）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rl_robustness_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"验证 DIF 对 RL 训练模型的鲁棒性。在 METABENCH 中分离 SFT-only、alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO)、 reasoning-RL (GRPO/PPO) 模型，比较 DIF 检测一致性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sft_only_cohort_n\": 312,\n      \"alignment_rl_cohort_n\": 477,\n      \"reasoning_rl_n_available\": 13,\n      \"dif_flag_jaccard_sft_vs_alignrl\": 0.72,\n      \"dif_flag_jaccard_sft_vs_full\": 0.85,\n      \"reasoning_rl_added_c_pct_change\": -0.4,\n      \"constat_auroc_on_sft\": 0.68,\n      \"constat_auroc_on_rl\": 0.53,\n      \"mink_auroc_on_sft\": 0.61,\n      \"mink_auroc_on_rl\": 0.47,\n      \"tost_equivalence_dif_retention\": \"p=0.08, inconclusive\",\n      \"bootstrap_ci_auroc_diff_dif_vs_constat\": \"[-0.05, 0.18]\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: DIF flag overlap across SFT/alignment-RL/reasoning-RL cohort compositions\",\n      \"Table: Per-detector AUROC comparison (DIF vs ConStat vs Min-K%) across model types\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"N=13 reasoning-RL 模型是不可克服的瓶颈。在 median 档审稿人接受 alignment-RL 部分但 认为核心 claim（DIF 对 reasoning-RL 鲁棒）未被验证。这个实验最终不进入 main body， 在 limitations 中提及为\\\"initial evidence, insufficient for formal claim\\\"。 GPU 预算 100h 大部分用于推理 10-15 个开源 GRPO/PPO 模型跑 MMLU，结果数据量不够 支撑统计检验。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，DIF 对 alignment-RL 模型表现稳定（Jaccard=0.72），因为 DPO/ORPO 不改变 NLL gap 结构。但 reasoning-RL 样本仅 13 个模型，严重不足以支撑任何统计结论。 将 13 个 reasoning-RL 模型加入 focal 队列后 C% 变化仅 -0.4pp，技术上\\\"稳健\\\"但 审稿人正确指出这不等于验证——13 个模型被 800+ 其他模型淹没。TOST 等价性检验 不显著（p=0.08），留下不确定性。传统检测器（ConStat、Min-K%）在 RL 模型上 AUROC 下降约 0.10-0.15，但 CI 宽，bootstrap 差异含零。 在 median 档这个实验被认为\\\"不够有力\\\"——N=13 reasoning-RL 的限制被视为致命缺陷， 整个 RL robustness 论述被降级为 future work 而非正式 claim。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"constat_perturbation_eval\",\n    \"description\": \"独立评估 ConStat 式 perturbation testing 在 MMLU 上的检测能力。 生成 200+ MMLU 题目的语义等价改写，比较原始/改写表现，FDR 控制检测。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_items_reformulated\": 237,\n      \"n_models_tested\": 50,\n      \"perturbation_detection_rate_overall\": 0.14,\n      \"perturbation_detection_rate_suspected_contaminated\": 0.23,\n      \"perturbation_detection_rate_clean\": 0.09,\n      \"fdr_controlled_detections\": 34,\n      \"mean_accuracy_drop_original_to_perturbed\": 0.031,\n      \"mean_accuracy_drop_suspected\": 0.058,\n      \"mean_accuracy_drop_clean\": 0.012,\n      \"constat_dif_flag_overlap_jaccard\": 0.11\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: ConStat detection rates by contamination status (Li et al. labels)\",\n      \"Table: ConStat vs DIF flag confusion matrix\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ConStat 在 MMLU 上表现不佳的根本原因是 MMLU 的 4-choice MCQ 格式限制了 perturbation 效果。改写后语义保持但表面形式变化有限，模型的正确率下降不够大。在 median 档 审稿人可能质疑 perturbation 质量，但更根本的问题是 ConStat 设计用于检测 verbatim 记忆而非 differential functioning，所以低 overlap 是 expected 而非 failure。 这个实验消耗 80h GPU 但产出有限，属于 negative-but-informative result。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，ConStat 式方法在 MMLU 4 选 1 格式上受限——perturbation 空间受限于 问题改写而非选项重排（MMLU 选项本身是固定的），导致 signal 较弱。 整体检测率仅 14%，在疑似污染 items 上稍高（23%）但仍远低于 DIF 的 31.3%。 accuracy drop 均值仅 3.1pp，信噪比低。ConStat 与 DIF 标记的 Jaccard=0.11 极低， 验证了两种方法捕获不同维度的信号——ConStat 检测个体模型的 verbatim 记忆， DIF 检测群体层面的差异功能。这个结果在 median 档被认为\\\"有信息量但不 compelling\\\"， 最终作为 baseline comparison 放入 appendix/supplementary 而非 main body。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"dvd_generation_variance_eval\",\n    \"description\": \"独立评估 DVD generation variance 在 MMLU 上的检测能力。 10-15 个开源模型每题生成 50 次 response，计算 generation variance，检测双峰分布。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_models_tested\": 12,\n      \"n_items_evaluated\": 12508,\n      \"bimodal_detection_rate\": 0.07,\n      \"bimodal_on_dif_c_items\": 0.09,\n      \"bimodal_on_non_dif_items\": 0.06,\n      \"variance_score_dif_c_mean\": 0.342,\n      \"variance_score_non_dif_mean\": 0.318,\n      \"variance_diff_effect_size_d\": 0.12,\n      \"dvd_dif_overlap_jaccard\": 0.04\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: Generation variance summary statistics by DIF category\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DVD 在 MCQ 上的理论限制是预期内的——generation variance 对 MCQ 格式本身不适配。 这 70h GPU 产出 negative result，在论文中仅作为一句话提及（\\\"DVD generation variance is designed for open-ended tasks and shows near-zero signal on MCQ benchmarks\\\"）。 审稿人不会挑战这个结论，但也不会因此给分。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，DVD generation variance 在 MMLU 上表现最差。4-choice MCQ 的 generation variance 本质上受限于离散分布——模型要么选对要么选错，temperature sampling 在 MCQ 上产生的 variance 主要反映模型 confidence 而非 contamination signal。 bimodal 检测率仅 7%，DIF-C 与 non-DIF items 差异极小（d=0.12），overlap Jaccard=0.04 说明两种方法几乎完全独立。DVD 设计初衷是开放生成任务（如代码生成），在 MCQ 上 先天不适用。在 median 档这个结果迅速确认 DVD 不适用于 MMLU 评估，实验结论明确但 对论文贡献有限。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ensemble_fusion\",\n    \"description\": \"融合 DIF + ConStat + DVD 为多信号集成检测器。2-of-3 majority voting 和加权融合。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ensemble_attempted\": false,\n      \"reason\": \"plan_003a 和 plan_003b 个体信号太弱，无法构建有意义的集成\",\n      \"constat_standalone_auroc\": 0.58,\n      \"dvd_standalone_auroc\": 0.52,\n      \"dif_standalone_auroc\": \"N/A (group-level, not model-level)\",\n      \"notes\": \"DIF 是群体层面方法，无法与 ConStat/DVD 在 item-model 粒度融合\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Ensemble fusion 的失败不是实验失败而是概念重构——认识到 DIF 和 per-model detectors 回答不同问题（\\\"which items function differently\\\" vs \\\"which models memorized\\\"）。 这个认识反而强化了 Claim 2（meta-critique），因为它揭示了粒度不匹配问题。 在 median 档，审稿人不会批评未做的集成，因为论文已经 pivot 到 diagnostic lens 叙事。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，ensemble fusion 因为两个根本问题而未完成：(1) plan_003a 和 plan_003b 的个体信号太弱（ConStat AUROC≈0.58, DVD AUROC≈0.52），集成无法从噪声中提取 信号；(2) 更根本的是，DIF 是群体层面方法（检测 item 在两个群体间的差异功能）， 而 ConStat/DVD 是模型层面方法（检测单个模型的记忆），粒度不匹配导致融合框架 概念上不连贯。在 median 档这个实验被正确放弃，论文叙事从 \\\"ensemble detection\\\" 转向 \\\"DIF as diagnostic lens\\\"，避免了强行融合不可融合的方法。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cross_benchmark_gsm8k\",\n    \"description\": \"在 GSM8K 上复制 DIF 分析，使用 GSM1K 作为 contamination ground truth。 三步：(1) GSM8K temporal DIF, (2) semi-synthetic validation, (3) GSM1K 相关。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"step1_gsm8k_temporal_c_pct\": 18.9,\n      \"step1_n_items\": 1319,\n      \"step1_sanity_c_pct\": 0.3,\n      \"step2_standard_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.818,\n      \"step2_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.517,\n      \"step3_n_models\": 33,\n      \"step3_pearson_r\": -0.478,\n      \"step3_pearson_p\": 0.005,\n      \"step3_spearman_rho\": -0.403,\n      \"step3_spearman_p\": 0.02,\n      \"step3_partial_r\": -0.385,\n      \"step3_partial_p\": 0.027,\n      \"step3_bca_ci_pearson\": \"[-0.714, -0.155]\",\n      \"step3_bca_ci_spearman\": \"[-0.687, -0.031]\",\n      \"step3_permutation_p\": 0.014,\n      \"step3_cook_d_max\": \"Deepseek-math-7b-rl\",\n      \"step3_leave_one_out_r_range\": \"[-0.537, -0.374]\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: GSM8K temporal DIF summary (1,319 items × 6,702 models)\",\n      \"Table: Semi-synthetic ΔTPR dose-response on GSM8K\",\n      \"Table: GSM1K correlation statistics with CIs (moved to appendix in median)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GSM8K 复制的 Step 1+2 在 median 档完全成立并进入 main body。Step 3 是 median 档 最大的弱点之一——N=33, wide CIs, causal ambiguity。在 rebuttal 中不应试图捍卫 Step 3 的 headline 地位，而应主动将其定位为 \\\"preliminary cross-benchmark evidence that motivates larger-scale replication\\\"。这样做既诚实又保护了论文的 credibility。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，GSM8K Step 1 和 Step 2 成功复制——temporal C%=18.9% 低于 MMLU 的 31.3%（合理，GSM8K 是单一数学领域，能力结构更均质），semi-synthetic ΔTPR=0.818 确认框架跨 benchmark 可移植性。\\n关键争议在 Step 3：r=-0.478 (p=0.005) 看似显著，但 N=33 导致 CI 极宽—— Pearson CI 上界 |r|=0.155 意味着真实效应可能很小，Spearman CI 上界 |ρ|=0.031 意味着几乎可以为零。在 median 档，至少一位审稿人指出：(a) N=33 严重不足， (b) GSM1K contamination gap 本身是 proxy 而非 ground truth，(c) 反向相关的 因果解释不唯一——DIF-C items 可能仅因为更难而使 contaminated 模型在上面得分低。\\n审稿人建议将 Step 3 从 headline results 降级为 supplementary evidence。这与 median 档的 \\\"GSM1K correlation is discounted\\\" 假设一致。论文将 Step 3 用作 \\\"suggestive cross-benchmark evidence\\\" 而非 \\\"confirmation of contamination resistance\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\",\n    \"description\": \"在 METABENCH MMLU 上拟合 bifactor IRT 模型（general factor + 57 subject-specific factors）， 选择 anchor items，通过 fixed-parameter calibration 进行 equating。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"bifactor_convergence\": false,\n      \"convergence_attempts\": 3,\n      \"partial_fit_5_subjects_rmsea\": 0.089,\n      \"partial_fit_5_subjects_cfi\": 0.71,\n      \"partial_fit_5_subjects_srmr\": 0.112,\n      \"full_57_factor_status\": \"non-convergence after 5000 EM iterations\",\n      \"anchor_item_selection\": \"N/A — model did not converge\",\n      \"equating_completed\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Bifactor 失败是 median 档 \\\"Claim 3 (regeneration) dropped entirely\\\" 的直接原因。 没有 bifactor equating，就没有 principled 的 anchor item 选择方法，整个 regeneration pipeline 缺乏基础。这个 negative result 对论文 framing 的影响是积极的—— 它迫使论文从 \\\"we can fix benchmarks\\\" 转向 \\\"we can diagnose benchmarks\\\"， 后者更诚实也更 defensible。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，bifactor IRT 在 MMLU 上面临两个结构性障碍：(1) 57 个 subject-specific factors 的参数空间巨大（12,508 items × 58 factors），EM 算法在 5,227 个 models 上 无法收敛；(2) 即使在 5 个 subjects 子集上部分拟合，fit indices 也不达标 （RMSEA>0.08, CFI<0.90），因为 MMLU 本身是知识测验而非心理测量量表——item 之间 的 local independence 假设被 subject 内的 topic clustering 严重违反。 plan_013 的 Q3 分析已显示 within-subject 有 11.3% 的 item pairs 违反 local independence。 bifactor 模型无法修复这个根本问题。实验被 kill 前仅消耗约 15h GPU（远低于 50h 预算）， 合理止损。在 median 档论文将此作为 limitations 中 \\\"empirical observation\\\" 的一部分， motivation for future multidimensional IRT work。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"item_generation_calibration\",\n    \"description\": \"为 DIF-flagged MMLU 题目生成替代题目，通过 student simulation 进行难度校准。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"experiment_executed\": false,\n      \"reason\": \"plan_005 (bifactor IRT) failed — no calibration targets available\",\n      \"dependency_chain_broken\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Plan_006 的缺失不影响 median 档论文质量——paper 已 pivot away from regeneration。 但审稿人中有一位可能会问 \\\"so what should practitioners do with these DIF flags?\\\" without replacement items, the answer is weak. This is one of the 1-2 claims needing softening in median tier — the diagnostic lens framing needs a concrete protocol (DIF audit checklist) to fill the actionability gap.\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，plan_005 的失败导致 plan_006 从未启动。没有 bifactor 模型提供的 item parameter targets，LLM 生成的替代题目无法与原始题目在 IRT 参数空间对齐。 仅靠 CTT difficulty (p-value) 匹配不足以保证 construct equivalence。 这 200h GPU 预算完全未使用。论文中不提及此实验（未执行 = 无结果可报告）， 但 regeneration 方向作为 \\\"promising future work\\\" 出现在 conclusion 中。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cumulative_bayesian_dif\",\n    \"description\": \"实现 Sinharay et al. (2006) 累积贝叶斯 DIF 先验。模拟 4 次连续 benchmark administration，展示累积证据下的 power 提升。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"simulation_only\": true,\n      \"single_admin_power_delta_10\": 0.42,\n      \"cumulative_2_admin_power\": 0.58,\n      \"cumulative_3_admin_power\": 0.71,\n      \"cumulative_4_admin_power\": 0.79,\n      \"effect_size_simulated\": 1.0,\n      \"n_per_admin\": 100,\n      \"prior_shrinkage_on_small_effects\": 0.35,\n      \"bayesian_fpr_vs_frequentist\": \"0.028 vs 0.042\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table (Appendix): Power by # administrations × effect size (simulation grid)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cumulative Bayesian DIF 在 median 档被视为 \\\"nice to have\\\" 而非必要。审稿人不会 批评这个 idea 本身，但会认为没有 real-data validation 就无法支撑论文 claim。 零 GPU 消耗（纯模拟），投入产出比合理作为 supplementary material。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，cumulative Bayesian DIF 是纯模拟实验，展示理论上的 power 提升： 单次 administration 对 medium effects (δ=1.0) 的 power 仅 0.42，但 3 次累积后 达到 0.71——超过了 MH 在 N=80, δ=1.4 时的 0.68。Bayesian shrinkage 还将小效应 的 FPR 从 0.042 降至 0.028。但这全部是模拟结果，没有在 METABENCH 真实数据上 验证（因为只有 2 个时间点，不够 4 次 administration）。在 median 档审稿人承认 理论价值但认为 \\\"simulation without real validation is supplementary at best\\\"。 这个实验被放入 appendix，作为 future monitoring framework 的理论基础。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"graceful_degradation_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"分析 benchmark 在 item 替换下的 validity degradation。 定义 validity metrics，模拟渐进替换（5%-50%），建立理论 bounds。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"replacement_items_available\": false,\n      \"degradation_only_analysis\": true,\n      \"removal_5pct_rho\": 0.9994,\n      \"removal_10pct_rho\": 0.9987,\n      \"removal_20pct_rho\": 0.9971,\n      \"removal_31pct_rho\": 0.9965,\n      \"removal_50pct_rho\": 0.9921,\n      \"shr_degradation_31pct\": -0.0015,\n      \"construct_coverage_31pct\": \"54/57 subjects retained ≥70% items\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table (Appendix): Ranking stability (ρ) and SHR as function of removal rate\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Graceful degradation 的核心发现已被 plan_017 部分报告。独立贡献有限但强化了 \\\"MMLU is massively redundant\\\" 的论点。在 median 档这作为 supplementary evidence 支持 Claim 4a (benchmark redundancy) 但不改变审稿评分。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，由于 plan_005/006 失败，无替代 items 可用，graceful degradation 只能分析 removal（不含 replacement）。结果高度积极：即使移除 31% DIF-C items， ranking stability 仍 ρ=0.9965——这直接支撑了 \\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\" narrative。 50% 移除后仍 ρ>0.99，证明 MMLU 有极大的 measurement redundancy。\\n但这个分析本质上与 plan_017 高度重叠（plan_017 已报告 ρ=0.996-0.999）。 在 median 档审稿人不会为 redundant results 给额外分数。graceful degradation 的独特贡献——construct coverage 分析（54/57 subjects retain ≥70% items）—— 是一个 small addition，放入 appendix。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"item_focused_trees\",\n    \"description\": \"实现 Tutz & Berger (2016) Item-Focused Trees，将 model release date 作为 连续协变量替代 categorical cohort DIF。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_items_analyzed\": 12508,\n      \"ift_flagged_items_pct\": 28.7,\n      \"ift_mh_c_overlap_jaccard\": 0.61,\n      \"ift_unique_flags_pct\": 4.2,\n      \"mh_unique_flags_pct\": 6.8,\n      \"temporal_trend_significant_items_pct\": 22.3,\n      \"linear_trend_dominant\": true,\n      \"nonlinear_trend_items_pct\": 6.4,\n      \"advantage_over_mh\": \"avoids arbitrary cohort boundary; captures gradual drift\",\n      \"disadvantage_vs_mh\": \"computationally expensive; interpretation less transparent\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table (Appendix): MH vs IFT flag comparison — 2×2 contingency table\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"IFT 确认 MH 发现的 robustness 但不改变结论。在 median 档审稿人可能欣赏方法论 thoroughness 但不会因此提高 novelty 评分。零 GPU 消耗，作为 supplementary 的 cost-benefit 比合理。\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，IFT 提供了 DIF 的连续视角——28.7% items 被标记，与 MH 的 31.3% 有 Jaccard=0.61 的重叠。IFT 额外发现 4.2% 的 items 有 gradual drift 但未达 MH 的 C 阈值（effect 在 B 区间逐渐累积），同时 MH 标记的 6.8% items 在 IFT 中 不显著（可能是 MH 对 cohort boundary 的特殊性敏感）。22.3% 的 items 显示 statistically significant 的时间趋势（非平坦 ICCs across release dates）。\\n在 median 档审稿人认为 IFT 是 \\\"interesting robustness check\\\" 但不构成独立贡献—— 核心发现（~30% items 功能不稳定）无论用 MH 还是 IFT 都成立。IFT 的计算成本 （每个 item 一棵 tree，12,508 棵）远高于 MH，但额外信息有限。 放入 appendix 作为 method robustness 证据。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"architecture_stratified_dif\",\n    \"description\": \"在 architecture-homogeneous (decoder-only) 子群上运行 DIF，检验 IRT 模型拟合 是否改善、spurious DIF 是否减少。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"decoder_only_n\": 5226,\n      \"decoder_only_pct\": 99.98,\n      \"non_decoder_n\": 1,\n      \"c_pct_decoder_only\": 31.3,\n      \"c_pct_full\": 31.3,\n      \"jaccard_decoder_vs_full\": 1.0,\n      \"rpb_mean_decoder\": 0.3993,\n      \"rpb_mean_full\": 0.3993,\n      \"lz_misfit_pct_decoder\": 98.0,\n      \"lz_misfit_pct_full\": 98.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: Architecture composition of METABENCH MMLU\",\n      \"Table: DIF results comparison — full vs decoder-only (identical)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Plan_010 的结果在 median 档是 strong defense against a weak attack——architecture heterogeneity 从未真正是个问题因为数据集本身就是 homogeneous。但作为 proactive defense（提前排除审稿人可能的 concern），这是 good practice。结果进入 main body 作为一句话 + footnote：\\\"METABENCH is 99.98% decoder-only (5,226/5,227); excluding the one non-decoder model yields identical results (Jaccard=1.0).\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 median 档，architecture stratification 产生了最 anticlimactic 但最 clean 的 结果：METABENCH MMLU 中 99.98% 的模型是 decoder-only，仅 1 个 encoder-decoder 模型 (AurelPx/Pegasus-7b-slerp)。移除它后所有指标完全不变——C% 相同， Jaccard=1.0，rpb 分布相同，person misfit 相同。这彻底排除了 architecture heterogeneity 作为 DIF 伪迹来源。\\n但同时暴露了一个 separate 问题：98% 的模型 |Lz|>2 表明 1D IRT 本身对 MMLU 严重 misspecified——这不是 architecture 的问题，而是 MMLU 57 subjects 的 多维性本身。在 median 档审稿人接受 architecture 不是问题，但可能追问 \\\"if 98% of models misfit the IRT model, how valid are MH results at all?\\\" 论文回应：MH 不依赖 IRT model fit，它直接条件化 total score，是非参数方法。 Lz misfit 是 IRT 的问题，不是 MH 的问题。这个辩护在 median 档被接受但留 lingering doubt。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"在真实 METABENCH response matrix 中注入已知 contamination，测量 DIF 检测力。 变化注入参数：contamination prevalence, exploitation rate, focal group size。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p0\": 0.326,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p03\": 0.548,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p05\": 0.834,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p07\": 0.99,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p10\": 1.0,\n      \"temporal_external_fpr\": 0.314,\n      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508,\n      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.674,\n      \"standard_mh_fpr_inflation_at_p10\": 0.616,\n      \"cross_subject_matching_fpr_stable\": true,\n      \"cross_subject_delta_fpr\": 0.0,\n      \"within_subject_fpr_inflation_p10\": 0.186,\n      \"dose_response_monotonic\": true,\n      \"n_clean_items\": 500,\n      \"n_injected_items\": 200\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table: ΔTPR dose-response across exploitation rates p ∈ {0, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 1.0}\",\n      \"Table: FPR comparison — standard vs cross-subject vs within-subject matching\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Semi-synthetic validation 在 median 档是论文中技术最 clean 的贡献。cross-subject matching 的 ΔFPR=0.000 结果是 elegant 的，提供了 concrete methodological recommendation。 但 \\\"niche\\\" 评价意味着这个贡献的 impact 被 discount——EMNLP 审稿人期望看到 broader implications for the NLP community, not just psychometric methodology refinement。 在 rebuttal 中应强调 framework 的 reusability：any future item-level detector can use this semi-synthetic protocol for controlled validation。\\n\\n在 median 档，semi-synthetic 实验是 Claim 3 的核心证据，成功展示了三个关键结果： (1) DIF 对 injected contamination 有明确的 dose-response（ΔTPR 从 p=0.3 到 p=1.0 单调增加），证明 DIF 能够检测 differential contamination； (2) cross-subject matching 完全消除 FPR inflation（ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 tested subjects），而 standard/within-subject matching 导致 FPR 从 0.30 膨胀到 0.62—— 这是 matching variable contamination 效应的直接证明； (3) 基线 FPR=0.314 接近 plan_001 的 temporal C%=31.3%，这不是巧合——它反映了 真实数据中已存在的 temporal DIF（注入在 existing DIF 之上叠加）。\\n在 median 档，至少一位审稿人欣赏 cross-subject matching 的 innovation（\\\"subtle and general insight about matching variable contamination\\\"），但另一位认为 semi-synthetic injection 过于简化（\\\"incorrect→correct flipping doesn't model real contamination mechanisms\\\"）。论文在 limitations 中 acknowledge 这一点。 Semi-synthetic framework 被一位审稿人视为 \\\"useful but niche\\\"——对 DIF 研究者有价值 但对一般 NLP 社区影响有限。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":276,"startLine":1,"totalLines":276}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RGGdeHKzZjVuwrgqcCfjNH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the data I need. Let me write the complete LaTeX paper. I need to:\n\n1. Cover all experiments from experiment_data.json\n2. Follow the paper_framing.md structure\n3. Follow the narrative guidance (median tier)\n4. Target \"够审\" quality — reviewable but not submission-ready\n5. Every quantitative claim must be backed by experiment_data.json numbers\n\nLet me plan the paper structure:\n\n- Abstract\n- Introduction (with \"instability ≠ invalidity\" framing upfront)\n- Related Work\n- Method (MH-DIF primer, semi-synthetic framework, cross-subject matching)\n\n\n- Experiments section organized around four main claims: temporal DIF patterns in real data, ground truth validation through meta-critique and perturbation analysis, semi-synthetic contamination validation, and downstream impact assessment through architecture stratification and degradation analysis\n- Supplementary results to mention or place in appendix\n\n: RL robustness validation, ensemble fusion approaches, bifactor IRT equating pilot, item generation calibration, cumulative Bayesian DIF, and item-focused tree methods\n- Key findings showing temporal effects at 31.3% detection rate with 0.318 false positive rate, strong enrichment signal at 0.96, minimal ability-based effects at 2.9%, substantial within-family model variation (61.3% for Llama2-v3, 38.7% for Mistral-Mixtral), weak domain generalization at 0.307 Spearman correlation, near-zero random baseline at 0.18%, and very low temporal-ability overlap at 0.014 Jaccard similarity\n- Still evaluating RL robustness validation results, then moving to limitations and conclusion sections\n\nNow examining the RL robustness metrics alongside SFT comparisons: the Jaccard similarity between SFT and alignment RL approaches is 0.72 with 13 available reasoning samples, but RL shows degraded AUROC performance compared to SFT across both ConStat (0.53 vs 0.68) and MinK (0.47 vs 0.61) metrics. ConStat's perturbation detection varies substantially by data quality—14% overall but 23% on suspected contaminated items versus 9% on clean items—with only 0.11 Jaccard overlap between ConStat DIF flags and other methods, while DVD's bimodal detection rate sits at 7%.\n\nContinuing through the remaining signals: DVD shows minimal overlap with other methods at 0.04 Jaccard, and the ensemble approach was abandoned due to individual signals being too weak. GSM8K temporal analysis reveals 18.9% contamination in step 1, with step 2 showing strong internal delta TPR (0.818) but weaker external validation (0.517), and step 3 correlation analysis across 33 models yields a significant negative Pearson r of -0.478 (p=0.005). The bifactor model failed to converge on the partial fit with 5 subjects.\n\nLooking at the remaining metrics: item generation wasn't executed, but the Bayesian simulation approach shows cumulative power reaching 0.79 across 4 administrations. Graceful degradation testing demonstrates strong robustness—removing 31% of items maintains 0.9965 correlation and removing 50% still preserves 0.9921. Item-focused trees flagged 28.7% of items with moderate Jaccard overlap of 0.61. The architecture is almost entirely decoder-only at 99.98%, with decoder-only contributing 31.3% of the overall signal and perfect alignment with the full model. Semi-synthetic validation is being examined for temporal and external TPR at the p0 threshold.\n\nNow I'm shifting to paper writing—I need to stay within the 8-page limit while softening Claim 2, moving GSM1K to supplementary materials, and incorporating the DIF audit protocol into the narrative. Let me start drafting the LaTeX.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6318,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10722,"cache_read_input_tokens":24108,"cache_creation":{